00:43:35,422 --> 00:43:37,361
Can we run a diagnostic from here?

506
00:43:40,639 --> 00:43:42,521
The transmitter has failed.

507
00:43:42,962 --> 00:43:47,305
But, we have to go outside to access it
and get Earth back online.

508
00:43:47,883 --> 00:43:49,594
Then I have to walk.

509
00:43:50,402 --> 00:43:51,472
Let me.

510
00:43:52,847 --> 00:43:53,888
No.

511
00:43:54,740 --> 00:43:58,080
After Rory, I'm best qualified
for walk and repair.

512
00:44:04,094 --> 00:44:07,584
This is not protocol. It's way
too risky for you go out there

513
00:44:07,665 --> 00:44:10,983
to fix the comms.
We don't know where Calvin is.

514
00:44:11,737 --> 00:44:15,182
Haven't had your Nitrogen detox.
Your health is my responsibility.

515
00:44:15,369 --> 00:44:16,934
- I'll be fine.
- Yep.

516
00:44:17,038 --> 00:44:18,473
What is it you say?

517
00:44:20,767 --> 00:44:22,353
"Slow is fast", right?

518
00:44:22,432 --> 00:44:25,266
- Yeah. "Slow to go fast."
- Yeah.

519
00:44:25,492 --> 00:44:27,799
Well, that's out the window.

520
00:44:27,952 --> 00:44:29,905
We can escape in our lifeboats.

521
00:44:30,077 --> 00:44:33,155
Earth is the responsibility.
Nothing goes down to the planet.

522
00:44:33,678 --> 00:44:35,779
It was stipulated in writing.

523
00:44:35,882 --> 00:44:39,055
What are you talking about?
What was stipulated in a writing?

524
00:44:41,636 --> 00:44:43,184
What was stipulated?

525
00:44:46,832 --> 00:44:48,860
David, first things first.

526
00:44:49,127 --> 00:44:53,003
When we're back in touch with Control,
we'll turn our attention to Calvin.

527
00:44:55,659 --> 00:44:57,136
Don't worry.

528
00:45:03,253 --> 00:45:08,033
Rate: 61 beats per minute.
Pressure: 97/53.

529
00:45:08,817 --> 00:45:10,536
I'd hate to see you relaxed.

530
00:45:10,817 --> 00:45:13,337
But she is relaxed.
Aren't you, Kat?

531
00:45:13,699 --> 00:45:15,739
Suit's running warm.

532
00:45:16,207 --> 00:45:18,538
Like Siberia in summer.

533
00:45:25,374 --> 00:45:27,331
I'm at the transmitter.

534
00:45:28,526 --> 00:45:30,978
Commencing on site diagnostics.

535
00:45:33,807 --> 00:45:35,235
It overheated.

536
00:45:35,705 --> 00:45:37,086
I can tell.

537
00:45:37,762 --> 00:45:38,771
How?

538
00:45:39,060 --> 00:45:40,646
I see scorching.

539
00:45:42,433 --> 00:45:44,420
I will pitch up the coolant levels.

540
00:45:44,939 --> 00:45:47,206
Is it possible Calvin
could've gotten into coolant?

541
00:45:47,370 --> 00:45:50,566
- Possible.
- We have to know.

542
00:45:55,870 --> 00:45:58,877
- There is the issue.
- Commander?

543
00:45:59,765 --> 00:46:01,210
It's bone dry.

544
00:46:01,525 --> 00:46:03,154
Calvin is a carbon-based organism.

545
00:46:03,290 --> 00:46:05,598
It needs food, water,
and oxygen. Just like us.

546
00:46:05,678 --> 00:46:08,899
We have to consider the possibility
it consumed the coolant for food.

547
00:46:08,931 --> 00:46:14,007
David, could you list all the water
sources aboard? Pure or otherwise.

548
00:46:14,117 --> 00:46:16,125
There is plenty of drinking water.

549
00:46:16,662 --> 00:46:20,329
There's coolant for the comms,
coolant for the CPU

550
00:46:20,784 --> 00:46:24,163
and there is coolant for the..

551
00:46:25,380 --> 00:46:26,503
Commander?

552
00:46:27,847 --> 00:46:30,808
Calvin just came out,
then grabbed to my suit.

553
00:46:36,865 --> 00:46:38,508
It's bigger.

554
00:46:41,659 --> 00:46:44,888
- It's trying to get in.
- Trust your suit.

555
00:46:45,028 --> 00:46:46,912
- Can it breathe out there?
- No.

556
00:46:47,121 --> 00:46:49,346
But it might be able to store
oxygen for a period of time.

557
00:46:49,557 --> 00:46:51,481
I'm closing the valve.

558
00:46:56,271 --> 00:46:59,637
- It's squeezing.
- Kat, Kat. Are you okay?

559
00:46:59,802 --> 00:47:02,153
Yes. The suit is thick enough.

560
00:47:02,262 --> 00:47:06,011
It's twisting up your leg.
Go, go to the airlock now.

561
00:47:06,284 --> 00:47:09,637
Oh, fuck this. I'm headed to the airlock.
I'll burn this fucker off!

562
00:47:09,832 --> 00:47:13,989
Kat. Focus on meeting David.
We will worry about the comms later.

563
00:47:14,988 --> 00:47:16,394
Sho?

564
00:47:21,087 --> 00:47:25,387
There is liquid in the helmet. Calvin
must have broken my coolant tube.

565
00:47:25,613 --> 00:47:28,899
- Kat, there is enough coolant.
- Yes I know.

566
00:47:29,174 --> 00:47:30,513
I know.

567
00:47:31,672 --> 00:47:33,894
David... meet me at the airolck.

568
00:47:34,315 --> 00:47:35,962
What? Yeah. Go, go, go!

569
00:47:36,017 --> 00:47:37,507
It's is squeezing harder.

570
00:47:37,621 --> 00:47:39,850
Calvin cracked the cooling
system in her suit.

571
00:47:40,132 --> 00:47:42,429
Commander. Calvin knows
exactly what he is doing.

572
00:47:42,524 --> 00:47:44,384
It's growing smarter.

573
00:47:44,806 --> 00:47:47,148
The liquid is blocking my vision.

574
00:47:49,428 --> 00:47:52,438
I don't have time.
I've got to jump.

575
00:47:52,594 --> 00:47:56,539
- Kat, the tether won't reach.
- I'm unclipping.

576
00:48:00,282 --> 00:48:03,832
- Kat?
- No comments. I've got to jump.

577
00:48:35,544 --> 00:48:37,480
David, I've taken care of the channel.

578
00:48:37,851 --> 00:48:40,875
She is not gonna tell you, but her
heart is beating out of her chest.

579
00:48:40,945 --> 00:48:43,979
She is drowning. So just be
prepared, she may not be rational.

580
00:48:44,011 --> 00:48:44,903
Copy that.

581
00:48:45,028 --> 00:48:47,701
Sho, I got no time for EVA.
Using the launch suit.

582
00:48:47,726 --> 00:48:49,123
- It's not designed for this.
- I know.

583
00:48:49,248 --> 00:48:50,451
There's not enough protection.

584
00:48:50,476 --> 00:48:52,433
- I know, don't worry.
- Kat is less than a minute out.

585
00:48:52,503 --> 00:48:54,008
- Check the airlock!
- What about decompression?

586
00:48:54,040 --> 00:48:55,061
- Just do it!
- It's gonna hurt.

587
00:48:55,086 --> 00:48:56,627
- Come on, do it!
- Is your helmet sealed?

588
00:48:56,652 --> 00:48:57,667
Sho!

589
00:49:08,425 --> 00:49:11,239
Guys, we're running out of time.

590
00:49:18,879 --> 00:49:23,452
- Kat. Kat.
- Don't swallow it. It's toxic, okay?

591
00:49:25,059 --> 00:49:27,484
I need you to help me open the valve.

592
00:49:28,273 --> 00:49:31,093
We'll do it together, okay?

593
00:49:32,860 --> 00:49:36,924
I'm gonna pull down, and you're
gonna go clockwise from your side.

594
00:49:39,392 --> 00:49:42,118
Okay? There you go.

595
00:49:42,402 --> 00:49:44,269
Good, good, good.

596
00:49:50,528 --> 00:49:53,903
Don't worry about Calvin.
We are gonna get you inside and get it off.

597
00:50:01,332 --> 00:50:02,592
Kat?

598
00:50:03,178 --> 00:50:05,603
No, clockwise from your side!

599
00:50:06,086 --> 00:50:09,461
Clockwise from your side!
Kat, come on!

600
00:50:09,613 --> 00:50:11,130
- Miranda?
- Yeah, I'm here.

601
00:50:11,221 --> 00:50:13,747
She's fighting me!
She's turned the lever the wrong way!

602
00:50:13,926 --> 00:50:15,441
Hold..

603
00:50:19,240 --> 00:50:21,373
Kat, you're fighting me Kat.
Come on!

604
00:50:21,537 --> 00:50:23,816
- We gotta do it together now! Come on!
- David?

605
00:50:23,841 --> 00:50:26,242
Kat, come on, please!
Kat, come on...

606
00:50:26,315 --> 00:50:27,251
- Kat.
- Look at me!

607
00:50:27,295 --> 00:50:30,053
- Kat!
- Just pull on the lever, okay?

608
00:50:30,210 --> 00:50:32,414
Kat, come on!
Come on!

609
00:50:32,485 --> 00:50:34,627
Just pull down on the lever!

610
00:50:35,413 --> 00:50:38,331
- David, she...
- Kat! Come on, you can do this!

611
00:50:38,382 --> 00:50:40,900
David, she's doing it deliberately.

612
00:50:42,734 --> 00:50:44,551
Come on!

613
00:50:45,087 --> 00:50:46,858
Kat!

614
00:50:47,648 --> 00:50:49,728
- Kat!
- David, stop.

615
00:50:51,301 --> 00:50:52,960
Stop.

616
00:50:56,531 --> 00:50:59,254
She's not letting
Calvin back in here.

617
00:51:00,817 --> 00:51:02,345
Kat.

618
00:51:06,879 --> 00:51:08,571
Commander...

619
00:51:34,188 --> 00:51:36,781
Kat. Kat.

620
00:51:46,970 --> 00:51:48,853
What's going on?

621
00:51:51,946 --> 00:51:53,977
What is going on?

622
00:52:27,546 --> 00:52:29,846
Guys, guys, do you copy?

623
00:52:32,671 --> 00:52:36,053
- Yeah, yeah I copy.
- Okay, okay...

624
00:52:38,367 --> 00:52:40,381
Just keep it together.

625
00:52:42,200 --> 00:52:45,504
We may have...
We may have an opportunity here.

626
00:52:47,005 --> 00:52:51,569
Calvin's ability to survive in that
vacuum and temperature is astonishing.

627
00:52:52,260 --> 00:52:54,802
But it can't live
much longer out there.

628
00:52:57,410 --> 00:52:59,406
Sho? Sho?

629
00:52:59,453 --> 00:53:02,571
Are you sure that we've lost
all communication with Earth?

630
00:53:03,540 --> 00:53:04,573
I am sure.

631
00:53:04,651 --> 00:53:07,032
Alright then.
We have to keep him out there.

632
00:53:07,102 --> 00:53:09,141
We have a new firewall.

633
00:53:11,110 --> 00:53:14,018
David. Can you see it?

634
00:53:14,133 --> 00:53:16,433
I'm seeing... Sho?

635
00:53:16,562 --> 00:53:19,127
- Yes.
- Can you re-flood the airlock?

636
00:53:22,140 --> 00:53:23,788
You tell me when.

637
00:53:26,842 --> 00:53:28,350
Okay.

638
00:53:38,802 --> 00:53:40,424
Did she close that valve?

639
00:53:40,533 --> 00:53:42,146
Oh, yeah, yeah she closed it.

640
00:53:42,339 --> 00:53:43,362
Ok.

641
00:53:45,197 --> 00:53:47,198
What are the ways through he get in?

642
00:53:47,822 --> 00:53:49,415
The thrusters.

643
00:53:49,923 --> 00:53:54,333
The manifolds in the thruster nozzles.
If he tries one, we could blast it off.

644
00:53:54,413 --> 00:53:56,199
But we'd have to know which.

645
00:53:56,514 --> 00:53:58,855
It's too dark.
I can't see anything.

646
00:53:59,105 --> 00:54:00,955
There must be some way.

647
00:54:02,603 --> 00:54:04,236
Thruster sensors.

648
00:54:04,392 --> 00:54:07,384
If it climbs in the nozzle,
the temperature should move.

649
00:54:07,455 --> 00:54:08,580
Should.

650
00:54:08,822 --> 00:54:10,077
Alright.

651
00:54:14,331 --> 00:54:16,838
- There!
- Thruster 2. Firing.

652
00:54:18,249 --> 00:54:20,969
Miranda, can you reach Tranquility?

653
00:54:22,893 --> 00:54:24,770
We missed! Cut it!

654
00:54:26,749 --> 00:54:29,310
Guys, it's heading toward that way.
No, no! It's heading towards the lab!

655
00:54:29,393 --> 00:54:29,807
It's fast!

656
00:54:29,849 --> 00:54:33,188
- I'm sorry, guys, I can't see.
- It's okay, we'll watch it.

657
00:54:35,501 --> 00:54:38,100
- Kibo.
- Thruster 3. Firing.

658
00:54:49,531 --> 00:54:51,070
Come on!

659
00:54:52,714 --> 00:54:54,498
Please, please.

660
00:54:54,790 --> 00:54:58,372
- Thruster 5. David, can you see it?
- Thruster 5.

661
00:55:03,429 --> 00:55:04,452
Sho?

662
00:55:10,533 --> 00:55:13,578
- What was that?
- We've burnt through too much fuel.

663
00:55:13,664 --> 00:55:16,007
- There.
- We were already low after the Pilgrim.

664
00:55:16,444 --> 00:55:19,007
Doc, listen. All this thrusting...

665
00:55:19,073 --> 00:55:21,314
We've placed ourselves
into decaying orbit.

666
00:55:21,338 --> 00:55:21,791
Shit.

667
00:55:21,876 --> 00:55:25,752
We'll reach atmosphere soon,
if I don't get us back to stable.

668
00:55:26,060 --> 00:55:29,791
And I'll need the rest of the fuel
to do it, if we even have that much.

669
00:55:29,816 --> 00:55:30,674
No. David?

670
00:55:30,801 --> 00:55:34,028
David, we can't risk Calvin riding
us down into the atmosphere. Ok?

671
00:55:34,068 --> 00:55:35,925
I don't know if it could
have survived it.

672
00:55:35,982 --> 00:55:37,353
We don't know.

673
00:55:37,378 --> 00:55:38,228
He's already gone well beyond

674
00:55:38,253 --> 00:55:40,852
what any living organism
should be able to survive.

675
00:55:46,946 --> 00:55:50,040
If it's between letting it in here,
or letting it down there...

676
00:55:50,265 --> 00:55:52,254
We let it in here.

677
00:55:52,754 --> 00:55:54,606
Where are you?

678
00:56:18,530 --> 00:56:20,749
We've just let it back in here.

679
00:56:25,397 --> 00:56:27,997
Moving us back into stable orbit.

680
00:56:33,891 --> 00:56:38,072
These creatures could have dominated
Mars for hundreds of millions of years.

681
00:56:38,152 --> 00:56:41,206
But now we know that they hibernate
for the loss of atmosphere.

682
00:56:41,482 --> 00:56:46,488
If we deprive it of air, retreat to
Tranquility and seal ourselves off

683
00:56:46,994 --> 00:56:49,361
And vent the rest of the station.

684
00:56:50,461 --> 00:56:53,633
Exactly.
No life support, no life.

685
00:56:53,875 --> 00:56:55,203
Right.

686
00:56:55,974 --> 00:56:59,181
Ok, Hugh and I will
sweep from quest east.

687
00:56:59,571 --> 00:57:00,642
And...

688
00:57:00,959 --> 00:57:04,625
You and Sho scout the poles and
lock off each compartment.

689
00:58:07,560 --> 00:58:11,334
This will take about...
four hours to vent all oxygen.

690
00:58:11,381 --> 00:58:13,783
- What do we do till then?
- We wait.

691
00:58:17,831 --> 00:58:19,167
You okay?

692
00:58:21,167 --> 00:58:24,539
Derry, look at me. You okay?

693
00:58:25,280 --> 00:58:27,094
I'm fine.

694
00:58:39,687 --> 00:58:42,742
I remember the day the
Challenger blew up.

695
00:58:43,977 --> 00:58:46,961
They took us out of school early.
I remember that day.

696
00:58:57,438 --> 00:58:59,454
It's hard to watch people die.

697
00:59:03,562 --> 00:59:05,155
Like...

698
00:59:07,847 --> 00:59:09,362
Fireworks.

699
00:59:11,619 --> 00:59:13,651
Up, up.

700
00:59:15,843 --> 00:59:18,938
A long, delirious, burning blue.

701
00:59:20,518 --> 00:59:24,367
I topped the windswept heights
with ease and grace.

702
00:59:28,592 --> 00:59:30,193
- Best eulogy ever.

703
00:59:32,177 --> 00:59:34,057
Rory'd say us:

704
00:59:34,668 --> 00:59:36,759
"Don't give me an eulogy."

705
00:59:38,263 --> 00:59:40,354
"Give me a parachute."

706
00:59:49,163 --> 00:59:50,770
He was my buddy.

707
00:59:55,466 --> 00:59:56,967
It's my fault.

708
00:59:58,731 --> 00:59:59,575
It's all my fault.

709
00:59:59,600 --> 01:00:02,712
Maybe it was your fault, maybe
it was my fault. Maybe.

710
01:00:03,151 --> 01:00:05,105
I know it doesn't matter, does it?

711
01:00:07,120 --> 01:00:11,357
Getting this thing onboard was a risk
and we knew it from the beginning.

712
01:00:12,564 --> 01:00:14,099
We took it.

713
01:00:14,618 --> 01:00:16,388
It's just surviving.

714
01:00:18,282 --> 01:00:21,879
Life's very existence
requires destruction.

715
01:00:24,346 --> 01:00:26,529
Calvin doesn't hate us.

716
01:00:29,339 --> 01:00:31,571
But he has to kill us

717
01:00:32,959 --> 01:00:34,631
in order to survive.

718
01:00:42,642 --> 01:00:44,071
Hugh.

719
01:00:44,342 --> 01:00:45,795
Hugh.

720
01:00:46,199 --> 01:00:47,759
Hugh.

721
01:00:49,041 --> 01:00:50,705
I don't know, I don't know.

722
01:00:51,880 --> 01:00:53,458
Hey, Hugh.

723
01:00:53,841 --> 01:00:55,702
It's fine.

724
01:00:57,726 --> 01:01:00,057
Sorry, because of all the...

725
01:01:01,729 --> 01:01:03,622
- Hugh?
- Hugh?

726
01:01:07,779 --> 01:01:09,229
There is no output.

727
01:01:09,697 --> 01:01:11,856
Kat. Get the defib.

728
01:01:14,468 --> 01:01:16,459
Get him right. Okay.

729
01:01:17,295 --> 01:01:18,792
- Get him down.
- I'll strap him in.

730
01:01:18,964 --> 01:01:21,134
- Take off the sling. Okay?
- Yeah.

731
01:01:22,275 --> 01:01:24,518
Sho, get the ACLS kit
and the defibrillator.

732
01:01:24,707 --> 01:01:26,145
Shit.

733
01:01:28,999 --> 01:01:29,999
Here.

734
01:01:30,171 --> 01:01:32,322
Prep the defibrillator
and get the shocks now.

735
01:01:32,402 --> 01:01:35,584
- 360 joules.
- Copy, 360 joules. Charging.

736
01:01:36,142 --> 01:01:37,493
Clear.

737
01:01:40,186 --> 01:01:41,320
- Charging.
- Still defibrillator in.

738
01:01:41,391 --> 01:01:43,040
Just stuck the shocks if you have to.
Go, 360!

739
01:01:43,065 --> 01:01:44,675
Alright. Clear!

740
01:01:47,992 --> 01:01:49,315
- Nothing.
- Go again. 360.

741
01:01:49,348 --> 01:01:51,434
- Go Again, hit him.
- Clear.

742
01:01:53,657 --> 01:01:54,510
Alright.

743
01:01:54,869 --> 01:01:57,807
- Okay output.
- Yeah?

744
01:01:58,312 --> 01:02:00,962
Ok, sinus rate: 98 beats pm.

745
01:02:01,253 --> 01:02:03,431
You really scared me there, buddy.

746
01:02:04,329 --> 01:02:05,522
David?

747
01:02:07,429 --> 01:02:08,694
David?

748
01:02:12,117 --> 01:02:15,116
- What is this?
- Stabilizing.

749
01:02:20,111 --> 01:02:23,603
- Get the plasma cutter.
- Calvin's feeding off his leg.

750
01:02:35,638 --> 01:02:37,289
Go. Get out of here.

751
01:02:41,107 --> 01:02:42,932
- Let's go!
- Come on!

752
01:02:43,973 --> 01:02:46,454
Miranda, let's go!
Pull away from Hugh!

753
01:02:46,587 --> 01:02:49,275
- We'll come back for him!
- Let's go!

754
01:02:49,509 --> 01:02:50,765
Sho!

755
01:02:55,913 --> 01:02:56,967
No!

756
01:03:01,622 --> 01:03:03,677
- Sho!
- No!

757
01:03:18,298 --> 01:03:19,775
Guys?

758
01:04:50,110 --> 01:04:53,029
- Calvin?
- We don't know where he is.

759
01:05:02,660 --> 01:05:05,164
- Where is Sho?
- He'll be fine.

760
01:05:05,189 --> 01:05:08,123
We stopped all oxygen venting
in the station.

761
01:05:19,178 --> 01:05:20,779
Lift me up.

762
01:05:30,551 --> 01:05:32,208
Oh.. Miranda.

763
01:05:39,834 --> 01:05:41,670
Up, up.

764
01:06:09,617 --> 01:06:11,483
I'm coming home, Mei.

765
01:06:46,212 --> 01:06:50,395
You know what I feel is not scientific.
It's not rational.

766
01:06:52,324 --> 01:06:53,877
I feel hate.

767
01:06:55,434 --> 01:06:57,033
I feel pure...

768
01:06:57,662 --> 01:06:59,064
fucking...

769
01:06:59,691 --> 01:07:01,672
hate for that thing.

770
01:07:13,689 --> 01:07:14,970
Calvin.

771
01:07:20,303 --> 01:07:22,173
How is that moving like that?

772
01:07:22,358 --> 01:07:25,076
He must have swallowed
the  marker on Derry's leg.

773
01:07:25,374 --> 01:07:26,506
Yeah.

774
01:07:29,460 --> 01:07:30,924
We can track it.

775
01:09:11,722 --> 01:09:14,586
Let's kill this thing!
Lifting "Zarya" now.

776
01:09:27,025 --> 01:09:29,793
Ok, it's suffocating. How long
do you think that's gonna take?

777
01:09:29,886 --> 01:09:30,840
I don't know.

778
01:09:30,917 --> 01:09:32,153
Proximity alert.

779
01:09:32,335 --> 01:09:33,627
Proximity alert.

780
01:09:33,803 --> 01:09:35,141
Proximity alert.

781
01:09:35,322 --> 01:09:36,681
Proximity alert.

782
01:09:36,807 --> 01:09:38,167
Proximity alert.

783
01:09:40,252 --> 01:09:41,253
They're coming.

784
01:09:41,621 --> 01:09:43,478
 Kat's distress call must have reached Earth.

785
01:09:43,775 --> 01:09:45,558
Right, where are they docking?

786
01:09:46,340 --> 01:09:50,325
- Shit. Looks like "Zarya".
- Jesus, that's where Calvin is.

787
01:09:51,573 --> 01:09:53,837
Station to "Soyuz".

788
01:09:54,462 --> 01:09:56,714
Station to "Soyuz", do you copy?

789
01:09:57,919 --> 01:09:59,976
Station to "Soyuz", do you copy?

790
01:10:00,448 --> 01:10:02,875
- Station to "Soyuz", do you copy?
- Try the flashlight.

791
01:10:06,564 --> 01:10:08,054
Come on, come on!

792
01:10:10,090 --> 01:10:11,856
They can't see this.

793
01:10:13,140 --> 01:10:14,889
Must be too reflective.

794
01:10:25,840 --> 01:10:28,852
Shit. What the fuck are they doing?

795
01:10:29,047 --> 01:10:29,977
David.

796
01:10:30,343 --> 01:10:33,935
David!
They are not coming to rescue us.

797
01:10:35,352 --> 01:10:37,897
- It's firewall 3.
- What?

798
01:10:39,605 --> 01:10:41,528
Firewall 1 was the box.

799
01:10:42,046 --> 01:10:44,090
The firewall 2 was the lab.

800
01:10:46,562 --> 01:10:48,539
The firewall 3 is the station.

801
01:10:50,326 --> 01:10:53,439
- But we have a new firewall.
- They don't know that.

802
01:10:54,061 --> 01:10:57,638
And if firewall 1 or 2 fail,
they have two choices.

803
01:10:58,532 --> 01:11:01,647
They can contain..
or they expel.

804
01:11:05,638 --> 01:11:08,224
They're pushing us out to deep space.

805
01:11:10,506 --> 01:11:13,247
They cannot risk
Calvin reaching Earth.

806
01:11:14,027 --> 01:11:15,691
It was my protocol.

807
01:11:16,708 --> 01:11:19,509
I insisted from the beginning,
and the committee agreed.

808
01:11:21,107 --> 01:11:25,400
They all put their names to it.
The list is as long as your arm.

809
01:11:26,975 --> 01:11:28,949
Look, protective firewalls is my job.

810
01:11:29,004 --> 01:11:31,816
And if we would have succeeded,
we could have gone home.

811
01:11:33,855 --> 01:11:35,374
And if we fail...

812
01:11:43,123 --> 01:11:45,211
Wait for me, Mei.

813
01:11:55,589 --> 01:11:58,440
Sho. Oh, he thinks it's a rescue.

814
01:11:58,684 --> 01:12:01,279
God! He's heading towards Calvin.

815
01:12:14,916 --> 01:12:17,899
Sho! Sho, can you hear us?

816
01:12:57,222 --> 01:12:58,503
Sho!

817
01:13:41,244 --> 01:13:42,642
Sho!

818
01:13:52,032 --> 01:13:54,083
- Sho!
- Take my hand!

819
01:13:54,193 --> 01:13:55,911
Don't let go Sho!

820
01:14:17,232 --> 01:14:19,511
No, don't, don't  let go!

821
01:14:21,326 --> 01:14:24,604
No! No! No! No!

822
01:14:25,029 --> 01:14:26,654
- No!
- Let go!

823
01:14:29,856 --> 01:14:32,154
No! Sho!

824
01:15:02,125 --> 01:15:03,862
Miranda!

825
01:15:10,099 --> 01:15:11,526
Miranda!

826
01:16:05,438 --> 01:16:08,171
The CPU is still up.
It's a miracle.

827
01:16:08,715 --> 01:16:10,058
We're..

828
01:16:10,391 --> 01:16:13,617
We're losing life support.
The temperature is dropping rapidly.

829
01:16:13,656 --> 01:16:17,345
Atmosphere's venting from everywhere,
and I don't know how to stop it.

830
01:16:17,400 --> 01:16:21,428
- Ok, how much time do we have?
- In here?

831
01:16:21,850 --> 01:16:24,164
Two hours, maybe an hour and 45.

832
01:16:24,500 --> 01:16:25,913
I need a...

833
01:16:26,530 --> 01:16:27,726
- What?
- Fuck.

834
01:16:27,836 --> 01:16:30,001
- Fuck. Fuck.
- What ? What is it?

835
01:16:30,818 --> 01:16:32,810
- What?
- We're...

836
01:16:34,021 --> 01:16:36,102
We're not moving into space.
The opposite.

837
01:16:36,204 --> 01:16:38,873
All that fucked up thrusting,
we are decaying again.

838
01:16:39,404 --> 01:16:40,713
What?

839
01:16:42,311 --> 01:16:45,064
Sho has a subroutine here.

840
01:16:47,855 --> 01:16:52,272
Without any correction in course, which
we don't have any fuel for anyway...

841
01:16:54,788 --> 01:16:56,983
We'll hit the atmosphere in...

842
01:16:59,820 --> 01:17:01,351
39 minutes.

843
01:17:13,641 --> 01:17:15,830
We're not gonna survive re-entry.

844
01:17:23,383 --> 01:17:25,113
But Calvin could.

845
01:18:10,899 --> 01:18:12,705
It's so cold.

846
01:18:37,427 --> 01:18:40,929
My father used to read this to me
when I was a kid.

847
01:18:46,352 --> 01:18:48,000
Goodnight, room.

848
01:18:51,156 --> 01:18:52,796
Goodnight, Moon.

849
01:18:54,318 --> 01:18:57,401
Good night, cow jumping over the moon.

850
01:19:01,386 --> 01:19:02,905
Good night, light

851
01:19:03,377 --> 01:19:05,178
and the red balloon.

852
01:19:12,699 --> 01:19:14,551
Goodnight, nobody.

853
01:19:41,308 --> 01:19:44,543
I remember when I saw
my first picture of Earth.

854
01:19:46,681 --> 01:19:49,493
And I asked my father
where all those...

855
01:19:50,321 --> 01:19:52,290
all those lines were.

856
01:19:53,790 --> 01:19:55,025
The borders.

857
01:19:59,934 --> 01:20:01,870
I really miss him.

858
01:20:22,495 --> 01:20:24,051
<i>"Good night, Moon"</i>

859
01:20:26,325 --> 01:20:28,467
<i>"Good night, stars"</i>

860
01:20:29,927 --> 01:20:31,662
<i>"Good night, air"</i>

861
01:20:36,929 --> 01:20:38,812
<i>"Good night, air"</i>

862
01:20:42,148 --> 01:20:43,515
Bait.

863
01:20:44,773 --> 01:20:47,002
Calvin needs oxygen to survive.

864
01:20:47,104 --> 01:20:50,851
With the O2 level so low in the rest of
the ship, it will drawning oxygen candles.

865
01:20:50,891 --> 01:20:52,677
We can use them as bait.

866
01:20:52,848 --> 01:20:56,317
There are two lifeboats, A and B.

867
01:20:56,689 --> 01:20:59,341
Both set to default entry trajectory.

868
01:21:00,005 --> 01:21:03,821
You press the button, they
autopilot themselves to the surface.

869
01:21:04,116 --> 01:21:08,580
Unless somebody...
somebody overrides them from the inside.

870
01:21:09,606 --> 01:21:13,288
I'll use the oxygen candles
to lure Calvin into boat A.

871
01:21:13,553 --> 01:21:17,331
I close the hatch, you press the button
to give me full manual control.

872
01:21:17,925 --> 01:21:20,685
If I can hold the stick
I can override the flight path.

873
01:21:20,765 --> 01:21:24,660
And I hold it long enough,
it will avoid re-entry.

874
01:21:26,317 --> 01:21:30,546
- You fly it into deep space.
- With.. With Calvin. Yes.

875
01:21:30,772 --> 01:21:34,651
Meanwhile, you get into boat B.
You press the button.

876
01:21:34,759 --> 01:21:37,781
and if there are no complications,
it'd take you back home.

877
01:21:37,967 --> 01:21:41,651
- No, we should lure Calvin together.
- Come on, Miranda.

878
01:21:42,155 --> 01:21:44,473
- It doesn't make any sense.
- Why?

879
01:21:44,872 --> 01:21:47,727
It is just that the lifeboats
are meant for one person.

880
01:21:48,231 --> 01:21:50,691
And this has been your plan all along.

881
01:21:51,601 --> 01:21:54,344
To make sure that creature
doesn't get to Earth.

882
01:21:55,227 --> 01:21:58,547
- Then I should be Plan A.
- No, I'm the pilot.

883
01:21:59,578 --> 01:22:01,321
You're Plan B.

884
01:22:02,249 --> 01:22:03,769
Listen, listen.

885
01:22:04,585 --> 01:22:06,200
I belong up here.

886
01:22:11,260 --> 01:22:15,964
I dont wanna go back down there
living with those motherfuckers.

887
01:22:19,764 --> 01:22:22,154
I need you to say you trust me.

888
01:22:24,275 --> 01:22:25,614
Yeah?

889
01:22:32,965 --> 01:22:34,191
I do.

890
01:22:36,142 --> 01:22:37,721
I trust you.

891
01:22:41,986 --> 01:22:44,549
Wait here. I'll signal you.

892
01:24:53,553 --> 01:24:54,947
Shit!

893
01:25:41,963 --> 01:25:43,230
Fuck.

894
01:27:02,600 --> 01:27:06,369
This is mission specialist Dr David Jordan
commanding "Soyuz" lifeboat A.

895
01:27:06,424 --> 01:27:08,932
22:33 UTC.

896
01:27:09,185 --> 01:27:12,721
The ISS has entered
catastrophic orbital decay.

897
01:27:12,932 --> 01:27:15,235
Initiating emergency
escape sequence in...

898
01:27:15,274 --> 01:27:16,009
5

899
01:27:16,489 --> 01:27:17,284
4

900
01:27:17,786 --> 01:27:18,474
3

901
01:27:18,944 --> 01:27:19,647
2

902
01:27:20,074 --> 01:27:20,840
1

903
01:28:00,005 --> 01:28:02,315
Come on, Miranda, get going.

904
01:28:18,338 --> 01:28:20,298
Initiating manual override.

905
01:28:49,357 --> 01:28:53,878
This is Dr Miranda North, black box
recording, in case of death upon re-entry.

906
01:28:54,571 --> 01:28:57,613
The creature killed four
of the six ISS astronauts

907
01:28:57,660 --> 01:29:03,300
with fifth, Dr David Jordan, presumed
dead, carrying it out into deep space.

908
01:29:04,552 --> 01:29:07,751
My five colleagues all sacrificed
themselves to maintain the firewalls.

909
01:29:07,776 --> 01:29:12,898
So, please, honor them for giving
everything to this cause.

910
01:29:13,094 --> 01:29:16,011
Mars life forms should be
considered hostile.

911
01:29:16,191 --> 01:29:20,434
Do not underestimate their intelligence
and their adaptive capabilities.

912
01:29:21,429 --> 01:29:24,132
Now, we did not learn how to
restrain or eliminate it...

913
01:29:24,194 --> 01:29:26,505
and if this creature
ever reaches Earth...

914
01:29:26,663 --> 01:29:29,566
use every available resource
to destroy it...

915
01:29:29,684 --> 01:29:32,719
or you will risk all human life.

916
01:33:33,186 --> 01:33:34,902
No, no! Don't!

917
01:33:35,101 --> 01:33:38,146
Noo! Noo!

918
01:33:44,089 --> 01:33:46,094
Noo! Noo!

919
01:33:51,802 --> 01:33:54,309
No! No!

920
01:33:55,662 --> 01:33:56,695
Don't!

921
01:33:56,906 --> 01:33:58,430
No, no, no!

922
01:33:59,270 --> 01:34:00,809
No, no, no!

